# Visual Design

Status: IN_PROGRESS
Milestone: M2 Approve the prototype direction
Dependencies: 01_PRODUCT_DECISIONS.todo, 02_REFERENCES_AND_PHOTOGRAPHY.todo

## Purpose

Make the site feel like a warm Indian home kitchen rather than a generic storefront.

## Tasks

- [x] Translate the supplied PDF and four references into an initial website plan.
- [x] Propose cream/deep green, restrained terracotta/pink and serif/sans typography.
- [x] Apply the later cursive/cute request: Dancing Script, blush/sage panels,
  scalloped edges, rounded controls, heart/bow details and a matching sharing image.
- [x] Propose a mobile-first, one-page MVP with a multi-page expansion path.
- [x] Define WhatsApp enquiries and quieter contact fallbacks without a shopping cart.
- [x] Choose a hero composition that respects the available photo quality and framing.
- [x] Implement mobile/desktop flow with actual cakes and restrained recipe-card styling.
- [x] Review typography, thin borders, spacing, photo rhythm and key colour contrast.
- [x] Implement the earlier three-section reduction; preserve it as history.
- [x] Restore original story/note under the hero in the approved four-section order.
- [x] Use transparent cake stickers with white contours, alpha-following shadows
  and no rectangular photo-card backing or overlapping hero badge.
- [x] Finish the new sticker/story browser and visual review in workstream 09.
- [x] Show visual design categories without manufacturing flavour/menu breadth.
- [x] Omit fabricated reviews, counters, availability, baking schedules and claims.
- [x] Review Bakingo/Creme Castle layouts and the four new visual references.
- [x] Prioritize readable text and clear navigation over decorative microcopy.
- [ ] Approve the visual direction and requested implementation scope with the user.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] The food stays primary; decoration does not overwhelm the actual photos.
- [x] Mobile image/text/actions fit the previously reviewed viewport layouts.
- [x] Revalidate full sticker bounds, readable labels and enlarged text for this revision.
- [x] Sparse content is edited honestly instead of padded into empty pages.
- [ ] The user has approved the prototype direction; file creation is not approval.

